# {{lb|en|quantum mechanics}} Any of the [[possible]] [[state]]s of a [[quantum mechanical]] [[system]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert D. Klauber|chapter=|editor=|editors=|title=Student Friendly Quantum Field Theory|url=|archiveurl=|archivedate=|edition=2nd|location=Fairfield, IA|publisher=Sandtrove Press|year=2013|year_published=2018|isbn=978-0-9845139-5-6|oclc=|volume=|section=&sect;3.11.4|sectionurl=|page=68|pages=|pageurl=|text=&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As you should (hopefully) remember, a '''quantum state''' in NRQM is an abstract vector in an abstract vector space, analogous to a physical vector in 3D physical space. The same thing is true in RQM and QFT.|t=|tr=}}

